// Keybindings for the Piper "Read MD aloud" tasks.
//
// IMPORTANT: VS Code / Cursor do NOT load keybindings from a workspace
// .vscode/keybindings.json automatically — keybindings are a USER setting.
// To activate these, open the Command Palette (Cmd+Shift+P) ->
// "Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts (JSON)" and paste the two entries
// below into your user keybindings.json. (This file is kept here as the
// canonical copy / source of truth for the project.)
//
//   Ctrl+Cmd+R  ->  Read the current Markdown file aloud
//   Ctrl+Cmd+S  ->  Stop reading
//
// Uses Control + Command (both physically present on every Mac keyboard) to
// avoid the Option/Alt key. Neither clashes with a default Cursor/VS Code or
// macOS shortcut. NOTE: make sure the Markdown SOURCE editor is focused (not
// the rendered preview, the Explorer, or the terminal) so ${file} resolves.
[
  {
    "key": "ctrl+cmd+r",
    "command": "workbench.action.tasks.runTask",
    "args": "Read MD aloud"
  },
  {
    "key": "ctrl+cmd+s",
    "command": "workbench.action.tasks.runTask",
    "args": "Stop reading"
  }
]
